    "<b>RAG</b> (retrieval-augmented generation) works in two steps. Beforehand, documents are split into chunks, embedded and indexed. When a user asks something, the system retrieves the most relevant chunks, puts them into the prompt, and the LLM answers from them - and can cite them. No retraining is needed; you update knowledge by re-indexing. Fine-tuning is better for changing behaviour or style, not for facts that change often.",
