    "To build one, start with 20-50 real cases, including edge cases and known failures. Read real outputs first (<b>error analysis</b>) to find the ways the feature actually fails, then define specific, measurable criteria. Grade with code where you can (exact match, valid format), with an LLM judge and a clear rubric for nuanced quality, and with humans for subjective or high-stakes calls.",
    "In production, pair offline evals with live signals: acceptance rate, edit rate, thumbs up/down, escalations and task completion, plus latency and cost per task. Re-run evals whenever the prompt, model or data changes, and agree launch thresholds with stakeholders before you see the results, not after."
